  "notes": "Step away from the city and the soundscape changes — but the city doesn’t completely disappear.\n\nThis short measurement captures the natural background of an open outdoor environment: a gentle breeze, subtle sounds from the surrounding landscape, and, far on the horizon, the faint but persistent acoustic presence of the city.\n\nIt’s an interesting reference for SPL Reference: quiet is rarely silence. Even when individual sounds are barely noticeable, together they create the acoustic baseline of a place.",
